###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The reweighting evaluates 540,000 downsampled frames (601 atoms) with each
# target MLIP in batches on GPUs instead of rerunning 54-window umbrella
# sampling; no timings are given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table 1 errors are in kJ/mol/A (forces) and kJ/mol/atom (energies), which the schema has no unit for; they are recorded with unit null and the unit in the label. MACE-MP0-D3 is the MACE-MP0 model with a D3 correction added at inference and is recorded as a second result of that run.
# - The fine-tuned model's 'test errors' (0.23 kJ/mol/atom, 3.65 kJ/mol/A; MACE-MATPES with post hoc D4 on the same test set: 1.48 and 6.22) do not state the error type (MAE or RMSE) and are not encoded.
# - The MACE-MP0, UMA and ORB-v3 checkpoints are not identified beyond their training data, so all universal models are paper-local runs. Authors are taken from the front matter (the manifest row has no DOI).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: paper front matter).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/majumdar2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

# --- BenchmarkResult labels (generated by artifacts/scripts/add_result_labels.py; do not edit) ---
